{"name":"Espresso Bar","hex":"#5b3f34","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"espresso","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A concentrated coffee beverage brewed by forcing hot water under high pressure through finely ground coffee.","A drink that includes espresso as an ingredient."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/espresso"},{"term":"bar","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Bavarian."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A solid, more or less rigid object of metal or wood with a uniform cross-section smaller than its length.","A solid metal object with uniform (round, square, hexagonal, octagonal or rectangular) cross-section; in the US its smallest dimension is ⁄4 inch or greater, a piece of thinner material being called a strip."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bar"}],"entries":[{"title":"Coffeehouse","blocks":[{"text":"A coffeehouse, coffee shop, or café, is an establishment that serves various types of coffee drinks like espresso, latte, americano and cappuccino, as well as other beverages. An espresso bar specializes in serving espresso and espresso-based drinks. Some coffeehouses may serve iced coffee among other cold drinks, as well as non-caffeinated drinks. A coffeehouse may also serve food, such as light snacks, sandwiches, muffins, cakes, breads, pastries or doughnuts. Many doughnut shops in Canada and the U.S. serve coffee to accompany doughnuts, so these can also be classified as coffee shops, although doughnut shops tend to be more casual and serve cheaper fare. In continental Europe, some cafés even serve alcoholic drinks, and in West Asia, coffeehouses may offer a flavored tobacco smoked through a hookah, called shisha in most varieties of Arabic or nargile in Levantine Arabic, Greek, and Turkish."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Caf%C3%A9_de_Flore.jpg/330px-Caf%C3%A9_de_Flore.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coffeehouse"},{"title":"Espresso","blocks":[{"text":"Espresso is a concentrated form of coffee produced by forcing hot water under high pressure through finely ground coffee beans. Originating in Italy, espresso has become one of the most popular coffee-brewing methods worldwide. It is characterized by its small serving size, typically 25–30 ml, and its distinctive layers: a dark body topped with a lighter-colored foam called \"crema\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Tazzina_di_caff%C3%A8_a_Ventimiglia.jpg/330px-Tazzina_di_caff%C3%A8_a_Ventimiglia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Espresso"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Palestinian_women_grinding_coffee_beans.jpg/500px-Palestinian_women_grinding_coffee_beans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Palestinian_women_grinding_coffee_beans.jpg/1280px-Palestinian_women_grinding_coffee_beans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Palestinian_women_grinding_coffee_beans.jpg/500px-Palestinian_women_grinding_coffee_beans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Palestinian women grinding coffee beans","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APalestinian_women_grinding_coffee_beans.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/MeddahOttomman.png/500px-MeddahOttomman.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/MeddahOttomman.png/500px-MeddahOttomman.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","